  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc76NlCj",
      "title": "interop: replace superseded Lagoon upgrade-transaction spec with the NUT bundle",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 927,
      "body": "`specs/interop/derivation.md` is Lagoon's derivation page (`protocol/lagoon/overview.md` links to it; there is no `protocol/lagoon/derivation.md`). Its \"Network Upgrade Transactions\" section still described the pre-bundle design and contradicted the generic mechanism specified in `l2-upgrades-1-execution.md`.\n\n## What was stale\n\n**Enumerated four individual deposits** generated from a nightly contracts commit (`71c460ec`), carrying a \"will be updated once a contracts release is made\" note. Lagoon activates via a 28-transaction NUT bundle (`lagoon_nut_bundle.json`).\n\n**Used the pre-bundle gas model** — `MaxResourceLimit + SystemTxMaxGas + UpgradeGasUsage ≤ L2GasLimit`, requiring every upgrading chain to set `L2GasLimit > 24_320_000`. That directly contradicts [iUBGL-003](https://specs.optimism.io/protocol/l2-upgrades-1-execution.html#iubgl-003-gas-limit-independence-from-block-gas-limit), which requires the allocation to be independent of the block gas limit and to work \"even if block gas limits are set to minimum values\".\n\n**Described the wrong activation timing** — CrossL2Inbox proxy initialization as a separate event on \"the first block at or after the activation block\" for chains in a multi-chain dependency set. The dependency-set-conditional transactions execute *in* the activation block, wrapping the bundle.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`specs/interop/derivation.md`** — describe the bundle, mirroring `karst/derivation.md`. Adds:\n\n- *Dependency Set Conditional Transactions* — the two wrapper deposits (`setFeature(INTEROP)` at 100,000 gas before the bundle, `ETHLiquidity` funding at 50,000 after) emitted only by chains in a multi-chain dependency set.\n- *Upgrade Block Gas Limit* — points at the generic mechanism and states that the allocation must not vary with the dependency set.\n\n**`specs/protocol/l2-upgrades-1-execution.md`** — the gas *bump* was specified, but not its reversal. Adds:\n\n- *Reverting the Allocation* — reconstructing the system config from the activation block MUST subtract the allocation, so the next block returns to the steady-state gas limit; the subtraction precedes any same-block `SystemConfig` update from the L1 origin; reconstruction MUST fail rather than wrap if the gas limit is below the allocation.\n- An allocation condition requiring the amount to depend only on the fork. The reversal is computed from the rollup config and a timestamp alone, so an amount that varied with the dependency set could not be reversed correctly — a chain would either leak the wrapper gas onto every later block or over-subtract it.\n\nThat last point is not hypothetical: op-node and kona had implemented opposite halves of it and disagreed by exactly 150,000 gas from the first block after activation. Fixed in ethereum-optimism/optimism#22216.\n\n## Incidental\n\n- `scripts/upgrades/interop.sh` generated the removed per-transaction sections and is now dead — it pinned the same nightly commit as the removed prose. Removed, and `scripts/README.md` (which used it as its worked example, and whose copy command already named a non-existent file) now walks through `upgrades/jovian.sh`, which is still on the generator path.\n- `karst/derivation.md`: the intent prefix is `Karst <index>: `, not `Karst: `; the bundle link's display text and href named different files, and it pinned a commit where the surrounding specs use `develop`.\n\n## Verification\n\n`markdownlint` 0 errors, `cspell` 0 issues, doctoc regenerated, filename lint clean. All cross-references checked to resolve. Transaction counts, gas values, intent strings, and orderings verified against the monorepo bundles and `op-node/rollup/derive` at `eaef4492c8`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-08-03T20:34:43Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-08-05T20:26:54Z",
      "additions": 84,
      "deletions": 276
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc76MEbd",
      "title": "lagoon: exclude post-exec transactions from DA footprint",
      "author": "sebastianst",
      "number": 926,
      "body": "Exclude Lagoon post-exec transactions (`0x7D`) from Jovian DA footprint accounting.\n\n- Specify zero contribution to block `daFootprint` and receipt `blobGasUsed`.\n- Explain the late-construction tradeoff and the bounded, linear underestimate for the version-1 SDM payload.\n\nContext: ethereum-optimism/optimism#22101\n\n## Validation\n\n- `just lint-specs-md-check`\n- `npx cspell specs/protocol/lagoon/post-exec.md`\n- `just lint-filenames-check`\n- `just lint-specs-toc-check`\n- `mdbook build`\n- `lychee` on `specs/protocol/lagoon/post-exec.md`\n\n🤖 *Co-created with openai-codex/gpt-5.6-sol*",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
